      <dt>Address</dt><dd>1600 Seven Seas Drive, Lake Buena Vista, FL 32830 (same campus as the Polynesian; confirm check-in location on your reservation)</dd>
      <dt>Size</dt><dd>A high-rise tower on the lagoon, opened in 2024, next to the Polynesian Village hotel and the older villas and bungalows.</dd>
      <dt>Rooms</dt><dd>Duo Studios sleep 2; Tower Deluxe Studios sleep 4; one-bedroom villas sleep 5; two-bedroom villas sleep 9; two-bedroom penthouses sleep 8. A single child under 3 in a crib does not count toward the maximum.</dd>
      <dt>Beds</dt><dd>Duo Studio: 1 queen-size pull-down. Tower Deluxe Studio: 1 queen and 1 queen-size pull-down. One-bedroom: 1 king, 1 queen-size pull-down and 1 single pull-down. Two-bedroom villa: 1 king, 2 queens, 1 queen-size pull-down and 1 single pull-down. Penthouse: 1 king, 2 queens and 1 queen-size pull-down.</dd>
      <dt>Getting around</dt><dd>Monorail to Magic Kingdom, and to EPCOT via a transfer at the Transportation and Ticket Center, via the Polynesian; boat to Magic Kingdom. Buses to Hollywood Studios, Animal Kingdom, the water parks and Disney Springs. Official dining text also mentions a walk from the Transportation and Ticket Center to the tower.</dd>
      <dt>Food</dt><dd>Wailulu Bar &amp; Grill in the Island Tower lobby, plus the Polynesian Village restaurants on the same campus</dd>
      <dt>Pools</dt><dd>Guests can use the Polynesian pools, including the Lava Pool. Whether the tower has its own pool is <span class="verify">[verify]</span>.</dd>
